IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `on-pit`
IMPORT `on-pit-dates`
IMPORT `on-pit-seat`

-- Taxation Act, 2007 -- worked cases from the seat of the individual. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on
-- stated facts. Expected values were worked by hand from the deposited text (the Act, and for 2026 the amounts in the
-- deposited T4127 and CRA programs page), never copied from the encoding's output. All the people are HYPOTHETICAL.
-- Where a case needs a 2026 spouse, age, pension or disability amount (not in a deposited text), the Act's written figure
-- is used as a HYPOTHETICAL input.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 2007. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 4 (1): which paragraph.
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 4 (1) applies to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph 1 -- resident on the last day, no income earned outside Ontario`
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 4 (1) applies to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph 2 -- resident on the last day, with income earned outside Ontario`
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 4 (1) applies to me` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph 3 -- not resident on the last day, with income earned in Ontario`
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 4 (1) applies to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable under s 4 (1)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 6 (1): basic personal income tax.
-- As written in the Act, tax base $50,000: 5.05% of $40,120 = $2,026.06; 9.15% of $9,880 = $904.02; total $2,930.08.
#ASSERT `the basic personal income tax` `the amounts written in the Act` 50000 EQUALS 2930.08
-- 2026 limits ($53,891, $107,785): $60,000: 5.05% of $53,891 = $2,721.4955; 9.15% of $6,109 = $558.9735; $3,280.469.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario basic tax` 2026 60000 EQUALS `answered` 3280.469
-- 2026, $250,000: $2,721.4955 + 9.15% of $53,894 ($4,931.301) + 11.16% of $42,215 ($4,711.194) + 12.16% of $70,000
-- ($8,512) + 13.16% of $30,000 ($3,948) = $24,823.9905.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario basic tax` 2026 250000 EQUALS `answered` 24823.9905
-- Nil tax base, nil tax.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario basic tax` 2026 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- 2025: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario basic tax` 2025 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `only the 2026 taxation year has deposited indexed amounts (T4127, January 2026)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9: non-refundable credits (2026). Basic personal: 5.05% of $12,989 = $655.9445.
-- With $4,000 of CPP contributions and EI premiums: + $202 = $857.9445.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 60000 4000 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 857.9445
-- Spouse with $3,000 of income, amounts $7,541 / $754 (hypothetical for 2026): 7,541 - (3,000 - 754) = 5,295; x 5.05% =
-- $267.3975; with the personal credit $923.342.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 TRUE 3000 FALSE 0 FALSE 60000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 7541 754 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 923.342
-- Spouse with $9,000 of income: 7,541 - 8,246 is negative: no spouse credit, only $655.9445.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 TRUE 9000 FALSE 0 FALSE 60000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 7541 754 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 655.9445
-- Eligible dependant with no income: B = 754 - 754 = 0; 5.05% of $7,541 = $380.8205; total $1,036.765.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 TRUE 0 FALSE 60000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 7541 754 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1036.765
-- Aged 65, net income $40,000, $2,000 pension: H = 15% of $7,720 = $1,158; age credit 5.05% x $3,178 = $160.489;
-- pension credit 5.05% x $1,228 = $62.014; total $878.4475.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 40000 0 TRUE 2000 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 4336 32280 1228 0 EQUALS `answered` 878.4475
-- Aged 65 with net income $70,000: H = $5,658 > $4,336, no age credit; no pension: $655.9445.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 70000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 4336 32280 1228 0 EQUALS `answered` 655.9445
-- Disability amount $7,175: + $362.3375 = $1,018.282.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 30000 0 FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 7175 EQUALS `answered` 1018.282
-- Other credits of $100 are added as they are: $755.9445.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 30000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 100 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 755.9445
-- Under 18 with the disability amount: not covered.
#ASSERT `What are my Ontario non-refundable credits` 2026 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 30000 0 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 7175 EQUALS `not covered` `the disability supplement for an individual under 18 (s 9 (12) (a)) is not encoded`
-- Under 18 supplement, core: M = 1,000: 5.05% of (7,175 + 1,000) = $412.8375.
#ASSERT `the mental or physical impairment tax credit` `the amounts written in the Act` TRUE 1000 EQUALS 412.8375

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 16: surtax. 2026 thresholds $5,818 and $7,446.
-- Gross tax $6,000: 20% of $182 = $36.40.
#ASSERT `the Ontario surtax` `the 2026 Ontario amounts` 6000 EQUALS 36.4
-- Gross tax $8,000: 20% of $2,182 = $436.40; 36% of $554 = $199.44; $635.84.
#ASSERT `the Ontario surtax` `the 2026 Ontario amounts` 8000 EQUALS 635.84
-- As written ($4,006), gross tax $5,000: 20% of $994 = $198.80.
#ASSERT `the Ontario surtax` `the amounts written in the Act` 5000 EQUALS 198.8
-- Taxable $250,000, credits $908.4445: gross $23,915.546; 20% of $18,097.546 = $3,619.5092; 36% of $16,469.546 =
-- $5,929.03656; surtax $9,548.54576.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario surtax` 2026 250000 908.4445 EQUALS `answered` 9548.54576
-- Taxable $60,000: gross $2,422.5245, under $5,818: none.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario surtax` 2026 60000 857.9445 EQUALS `answered` 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 21.1: LIFT.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for LIFT` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Confined to a prison over December 31 and the first 179 days: not eligible ((2) (g)).
#ASSERT (`Do I qualify for LIFT` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not resident in Canada at the beginning of the year ((1)): not eligible.
#ASSERT (`Do I qualify for LIFT` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Employment income $40,000, both incomes $40,000: D = $875; E = 5% of $7,500 = $375; $500.
#ASSERT `What is my LIFT credit` TRUE 40000 40000 40000 EQUALS 500
-- Own $30,000, family $70,000: E = 5% of the greater of 0 and $5,000 = $250; $625.
#ASSERT `What is my LIFT credit` TRUE 30000 30000 70000 EQUALS 625
-- Employment income $10,000: D = the lesser of $875 and $505 = $505; E nil; $505.
#ASSERT `What is my LIFT credit` TRUE 10000 10000 10000 EQUALS 505
-- Employment income $60,000: E = 5% of $27,500 = $1,375 > $875: nil.
#ASSERT `What is my LIFT credit` TRUE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS 0
-- Not eligible: nil.
#ASSERT `What is my LIFT credit` FALSE 20000 20000 20000 EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 24: Ontario Health Premium.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 20000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 25000 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 36000 EQUALS 300
-- $38,000: $300 + 6% of $2,000 = $420.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 38000 EQUALS 420
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 48000 EQUALS 450
-- $48,400: $450 + 25% of $400 = $550.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 48400 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 60000 EQUALS 600
-- $72,500: $600 + 25% of $500 = $725.
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 72500 EQUALS 725
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 200000 EQUALS 750
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` TRUE 210000 EQUALS 900
-- Not resident in Ontario on December 31 (s 4 (1) para 3 or none): no premium (s 24 (1)).
#ASSERT `What is my Ontario Health Premium` FALSE 60000 EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5 (1) with s 4 (3): the total for 2026.
-- A: single, taxable $60,000, credits $857.9445. Division B: gross $2,422.5245, no surtax, reduction 2 x $300 = $600 less
-- than the tax: nil; LIFT nil (E $1,375). Health Premium $600. Total $3,022.5245.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `answered` 3022.5245
-- B: low-income worker, taxable and employment income $25,000, credits $731.6945. Basic $1,262.50; tax otherwise payable
-- $530.8055; reduction $600 - $530.8055 = $69.1945; LIFT $875: Division B nil. Health Premium $300. Total $300.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 25000 731.6945 0 0 0 0 FALSE 25000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 25000 25000 25000 EQUALS `answered` 300
-- C: taxable $250,000, credits $908.4445: $23,915.546 + surtax $9,548.54576 = $33,464.09176; premium $900. Total
-- $34,364.09176.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 250000 908.4445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 250000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 250000 250000 250000 EQUALS `answered` 34364.09176
-- D: single parent, one child, taxable $45,000 (pension, no employment income), credits $700. Basic $2,272.50; gross
-- $1,572.50; personal amount $300 + $554 = $854; reduction $1,708 - $1,572.50 = $135.50; Division B $1,437; premium $300 +
-- 6% of $2,500 = $450. Total $1,887.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 45000 700 0 0 1 0 FALSE 45000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 45000 45000 EQUALS `answered` 1887
-- E: the same, living with a spouse whose income ($50,000) is higher: the child may not be included (s 20 (2)); the
-- reduction is 2 x $300 = $600 < $1,572.50: nil. Division B $1,572.50, premium $450, total $2,022.50.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 45000 700 0 0 1 0 TRUE 45000 50000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 45000 95000 EQUALS `answered` 2022.5
-- F: the same as D but a bankrupt in the year: no reduction (s 20 (9) (e)). Total $1,572.50 + $450 = $2,022.50.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 45000 700 0 0 1 0 FALSE 45000 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 45000 45000 EQUALS `answered` 2022.5
-- G: as A with a $100 dividend tax credit and $50 foreign tax credit: $2,422.5245 - $100 - $50 = $2,272.5245; + $600.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 100 50 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `answered` 2872.5245
-- Not covered: not resident on December 31; income outside Ontario; 2025; split income; minimum tax; ss 14, 15.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `only an individual resident in Ontario on the last day of the year is encoded (s 4 (1) para 1)`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `income earned outside Ontario brings in the Ontario allocation factor (s 4 (1) para 2, s 6 (2)), which is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2025 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `only the 2026 taxation year has deposited indexed amounts (T4127, January 2026)`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `split income (s 12.1) is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `minimum tax (s 19.2) is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 60000 857.9445 0 0 0 0 FALSE 60000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60000 60000 60000 EQUALS `not covered` `the overseas employment and minimum tax carryover credits (ss 14, 15) are not encoded`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 115: instalments. 2026 is not a leap year: March 15 is day 73, June 15 day 165, September 15 day 257, December 15 day
-- 348 counted from January 1.
#ASSERT `days from the start of` 2026 `to` 15 3 EQUALS 73
#ASSERT `days from the start of` 2026 `to` 15 12 EQUALS 348
#ASSERT `When are my Ontario instalments due` 2026 FALSE EQUALS (LIST Date 15 3 2026, Date 15 6 2026, Date 15 9 2026, Date 15 12 2026)
#ASSERT `When are my Ontario instalments due` 2026 TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
-- All four paid on time: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay Ontario instalments` 2026 FALSE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` `pay the March 15 instalment` 70, EVENT `the individual` `pay the June 15 instalment` 160, EVENT `the individual` `pay the September 15 instalment` 250, EVENT `the individual` `pay the December 15 instalment` 340) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Relieved by ITA s 156.1 (s 115 (7)): nothing owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay Ontario instalments` 2026 TRUE) 0 (LIST) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY `the individual`, "no instalment paid on or before December 15 (s 115 (1) (a))" -- the December
-- instalment comes on day 360, after day 348.
#TRACE `the duty to pay Ontario instalments` 2026 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay the March 15 instalment` AT 70
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay the June 15 instalment` AT 160
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay the September 15 instalment` AT 250
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay the December 15 instalment` AT 360

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 104: the Ontario child benefit. July 2026 to June 2027: A = $1,760 (finding 6), threshold $26,865.
-- One child, income under the threshold: $1,760 / 12 a month, which the CRA page prints as "up to $146.66".
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 20000 EQUALS `answered` (1760 DIVIDED BY 12)
#ASSERT (`the Ontario child benefit for the month` `the OCB amounts for July 2026 to June 2027` TRUE 1 0 20000) GREATER THAN 146.66
#ASSERT (`the Ontario child benefit for the month` `the OCB amounts for July 2026 to June 2027` TRUE 1 0 20000) LESS THAN 146.67
-- Two children, $40,000: C = 8% of $13,135 = $1,050.80; ($3,520 - $1,050.80) / 12 = $2,469.20 / 12.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 1 2027 TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 0 40000 EQUALS `answered` (2469.2 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- One child, $48,865: C = $1,760: nil.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 48865 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- One child, $48,846.25: C = $1,758.50; $1.50 for the year is under $2.01: nil (s 104 (6.2)).
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 48846.25 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- One child, shared custody, $26,865: (A + B) / 2 with A = $1,760 / 12, B nil: $1,760 / 24.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 9 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 1 26865 EQUALS `answered` (1760 DIVIDED BY 24)
-- Not resident in Ontario on the first day of the month: nil.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 9 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 0 20000 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- No Canada child benefit for the month: nil.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 9 2026 FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 0 20000 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- June 2026: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit a month` 6 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 20000 EQUALS `not covered` `only benefit months from July 2026 to June 2027 have deposited indexed amounts`
-- As written in the Act ($1,310, $20,000): one child, $20,000: $1,310 / 12.
#ASSERT `the Ontario child benefit for the month` `the OCB amounts written in the Act` TRUE 1 0 20000 EQUALS (1310 DIVIDED BY 12)

-- s 104 (8), (9): repayment.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit must I repay` 500 400 EQUALS 100
-- $1.50 or $2 over: not more than $2, nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit must I repay` 401.5 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much Ontario child benefit must I repay` 402 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to repay an Ontario child benefit overpaid` 500 400) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` `repay the excess Ontario child benefit to the Ontario Minister` 30) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to repay an Ontario child benefit overpaid` 402 400) 0 (LIST) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 103.8: the Ontario sales tax credit, July 2026 to June 2027: $378 a person; $29,047 single, $36,309 family.
-- Single, $20,000: $378 / 12 = $31.50.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 20000 EQUALS `answered` 31.5
-- Single, $35,000: 4% of $5,953 = $238.12; ($378 - $238.12) / 12 = $139.88 / 12.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 35000 EQUALS `answered` (139.88 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- Couple with two children, $50,000: 4 x $378 = $1,512; 4% of $13,691 = $547.64; $964.36 / 12.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 3 2027 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 0 FALSE 50000 EQUALS `answered` (964.36 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- Single parent, one child, $30,000 (under $36,309): $756 / 12 = $63.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE 30000 EQUALS `answered` 63
-- The same child in shared custody: D = $63; E as single with no child: ($378 - 4% of $953) / 12 = $339.88 / 12;
-- (D + E) / 2 = ($756 + $339.88) / 24 = $1,095.88 / 24.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 1 FALSE 30000 EQUALS `answered` (1095.88 DIVIDED BY 24)
-- Not eligible for the federal GST/HST credit: nil.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 20000 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- A senior with a spouse: not covered (s 103.8 (5)). A senior living alone: covered.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 20000 EQUALS `not covered` `the seniors' income threshold of s 103.8 (5) is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much Ontario sales tax credit a month` 7 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE 20000 EQUALS `answered` 31.5
-- As written in the Act ($260, $20,000): single, $20,000: $260 / 12.
#ASSERT `the Ontario sales tax credit for the month` `the OSTC amounts written in the Act` TRUE FALSE 0 0 20000 EQUALS (260 DIVIDED BY 12)
